  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 256 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nDry and seasonally warm conditions will continue through the \nremainder of the holiday weekend before the upper level ridge begins \nbuilding back into the area. While LREF probabilities of heat \nindices greater than 100 degrees are low (10-20%), high temperatures \non Tuesday will be around 5-10 degrees above normal. These high \ntemperatures will continue on Wednesday, though there is some \nuncertainty due to the potential for a front to move through the \narea Tuesday night into Wednesday morning, bringing in rain and \nlingering cloud cover that could temper highs on Wednesday. \n\nWednesday night into Thursday, another boundary will sweep through \nthe area. Much of guidance keeps this boundary dry, owing in part to \nthe frontal passage on Wednesday sweeping out some of the moisture. \nAs northwest flow returns to the region, near-normal temperatures \nwill return through the end of the work week.",
